WEBVTT

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:16.820
This is Oracle Guardian, Apollon!

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.490
And this is Lozenge.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:23.230
Cut it out, Sub-manager!

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.150
<i>Great!</i> And after Dad put it together for me!

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:30.860
Bad cat!

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.840
Mom and Dad sure are late...

00:00:36.340 --> 00:00:40.230
They promised to teach me how 
to play Cardfight today...

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:43.800
Misaki! Something terrible's happened!

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.600
It's your Mom and Dad...!

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:03.940
Another memory from then...

00:02:41.920 --> 00:02:43.510
Oww...

00:02:45.190 --> 00:02:48.830
Oh, I'm okay. It's not bad.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:59.120
Misaki! Are you awake?!

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:02.150
Breakfast is ready!

00:03:02.150 --> 00:03:04.950
If you don't eat a good breakfast, 
it'll stunt your growth!

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.260
How old does Shin think I am?

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:10.640
I'll be right there!

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.670
I just want tea and toast this morning!

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:16.670
What am I gonna do with 
this rice and miso soup?!

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:21.700
The Indelible Memory

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.860
Congratulations

00:03:28.430 --> 00:03:31.020
Yep, that was really something.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.390
I'm proud of it, too.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:35.440
What do you think?

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.940
What are you gonna do with those?

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:41.000
Put 'em up at the front of 
the store. Good idea, right?

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:44.450
But do I use "Congratulations, 
Q4, on Making the Nationals!"...

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:49.460
or "Congratulations on Making the 
Nationals, Q4"? I just can't decide!

00:03:49.460 --> 00:03:51.160
You're making too much of it.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:55.980
Shin is like my dad that way...

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:58.400
I phrased it really good, didn't I?

00:03:59.320 --> 00:04:01.680
This is a nice picture.

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:03.490
Let's hang it up in the store, Misaki.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.910
Sub-manager! What are you doing?!

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:10.340
"Congratulations"...

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.270
"Q4"...

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:12.180
"on Making the National"...

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.500
"Dog Show"...

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:16.230
Well, that's what it says!

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:17.550
See?

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:20.040
Note: The paw print turned "tournament" into "dog show".

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:20.540
He's right!

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:22.390
But that's...

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.950
This is bad. This is <i>really</i> bad!

00:04:28.950 --> 00:04:30.270
What's bad?

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.160
Ren Suzugamori.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:43.010
Ren Suzugamori...

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.020
He represents the highest 
level of the Nationals.

00:04:46.020 --> 00:04:49.120
And there may be lots more Vanguard 
Fighters playing at his level.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.840
Like they say, if you see one cockroach, 
there are 30 behind the wall.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.550
They don't say that about <i>people</i>...

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:59.280
Oh, no... Among a lot of other 
fighters like him, what can I do...?

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:00.490
That's it!

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:01.300
Here!

00:05:02.790 --> 00:05:03.710
What?

00:05:03.710 --> 00:05:05.630
The deck he used.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.360
We'll start by thoroughly studying the enemy!

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.760
Not bad for a little brat.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.970
Who you callin' "little brat", Lose-umi?!

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:14.510
Kamui...

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:15.970
Morikawa...

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:19.940
This is wrong.

00:05:20.460 --> 00:05:24.910
There should be one more Cocoa and 
there were two Chocolats, not three.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:27.000
Now that you mention it...

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.670
Aside from that, he only used this 
deck once, at that card shop, right?

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:32.760
I don't think it'll be of any help.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:35.480
I-I see...

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:38.990
Then, how about this?!

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:44.300
A Cardfighter's individuality and 
technique can make up for experience.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:48.950
I think bringing that out more will be 
tied to making Team Q4 even stronger.

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:51.210
That's a really good idea!

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:52.230
Aw, shucks!

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:53.790
All my experience...

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.740
and everything I've been doing 
hasn't been for nothin'!

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:56.060
And I...

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:57.900
Punk... How old do you think you are...?

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:59.370
have been doing my best 
with all kinds of things.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.370
Now, now...

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:04.190
In fact, I guess you could say that for 
Q4, I'm the "brains behind the surgery".

00:06:05.620 --> 00:06:06.840
"Behind the operation"?

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:09.980
Y-Yeah, that's it! The brains 
behind the operation!

00:06:09.980 --> 00:06:10.590
Right.

00:06:11.490 --> 00:06:12.320
Shut up!

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:14.180
I didn't say anything yet!

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:17.240
A-Anyway, please get started!

00:06:17.240 --> 00:06:20.980
Everyone, find a fighting style 
that you think you're good at!

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.150
That I'm good at...?

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:27.040
My fighting style...

00:06:36.510 --> 00:06:38.180
No grade 2s...

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:40.390
I'm going to redraw.

00:06:40.390 --> 00:06:41.440
Me too.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:45.080
Good move. Can't do much with only one grade 3...

00:06:45.080 --> 00:06:46.050
<i>That's</i> why?!

00:06:49.750 --> 00:06:51.760
No good...

00:06:54.440 --> 00:06:56.890
Libra...Amaterasu...

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.260
Milk...

00:06:58.620 --> 00:07:02.340
Dad, this is "Weather Girl, Milk", right?!

00:07:03.130 --> 00:07:05.910
And this is, um...

00:07:11.580 --> 00:07:12.720
Misaki...?

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.740
Can we start?

00:07:17.060 --> 00:07:18.300
S-Sure.

00:07:18.980 --> 00:07:20.920
Oh, no... Not again...

00:07:22.470 --> 00:07:24.660
Stand up, Vanguard!

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.270
Barcgal!

00:07:29.930 --> 00:07:31.400
Lozenge Magus!

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:36.720
I go first.

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.140
I ride Weather Girl, Milk.

00:07:43.260 --> 00:07:45.310
Lozenge moves to Rear-guard.

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:47.690
That ends my turn.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:50.030
It's my turn!

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:53.950
It's not grade 2.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:57.460
At this rate, I won't be 
able to use a grade 3.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.060
What should I do?

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:03.420
Oh, that's right! If I use 
the method I did before...

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:05.240
I ride Wingal!

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:08.100
I move Barcgal to the rear-guard!

00:08:08.100 --> 00:08:12.300
And then I use Barcgal's skill 
to superior-call Flogal!

00:08:15.550 --> 00:08:18.050
Next, I call Elaine!

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.350
I attack Milk with Wingal!

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:30.600
Drive check!

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:34.670
Damage check.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.910
I attack Milk with Elaine, boosted by Flogal!

00:08:48.270 --> 00:08:49.740
Damage check.

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:52.330
I end my turn.

00:08:52.330 --> 00:08:53.880
It's my turn.

00:08:54.750 --> 00:08:56.780
I ride Maiden of Libra.

00:08:57.640 --> 00:09:00.790
And then I call the Oracle Guardian, Gemini.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.450
I attack Elaine with Libra!

00:09:06.290 --> 00:09:09.050
Gemini's boost gives her +8000 power!

00:09:16.020 --> 00:09:18.110
Elaine retires from the field.

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:20.480
That's the end of my turn.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:22.860
Her turn's over already?!

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:24.610
Even though she's probably got 
more good cards in her hand...

00:09:24.610 --> 00:09:28.100
She shouldn't be stingy, but 
get 'em all out there, right?

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:29.260
Your voice is too loud...

00:09:32.790 --> 00:09:33.590
Huh?

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.350
She didn't yell at you...

00:09:35.730 --> 00:09:37.860
A bare minimum of calling...

00:09:37.860 --> 00:09:41.540
And she didn't attack my 
Vanguard, but the rear-guard...

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:44.140
Thanks to that, I didn't 
take any damage, but...

00:09:45.130 --> 00:09:46.300
Misaki...

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:49.030
What exactly are you trying to do?

00:09:52.550 --> 00:09:54.680
I mustn't think about anything else...

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:57.470
I have to concentrate on this fight...

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.120
It's my turn.

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:24.510
This isn't grade 2 either...

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:28.620
Then I'll use Barcgal to bring out Llew...

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:31.730
and use Llew's skill to bring forth Blaster Blade.

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:35.730
Oh, no! I can't pay the cost that's 
needed for the Counterblast!

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:38.860
Don't tell me...

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.210
I attack Elaine with Libra!

00:10:48.340 --> 00:10:50.530
Elaine leaves the field.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:55.000
Misaki guessed what I was going to do?

00:10:55.000 --> 00:10:58.980
So you <i>did</i> intend to use 
Barcgal and Llew's combination skill...

00:11:00.020 --> 00:11:05.710
Even without drawing a grade 2 unit, you 
could use that skill to bring out Blaster Blade.

00:11:05.710 --> 00:11:07.810
Like in the final match of 
the regional tournament...

00:11:08.040 --> 00:11:09.850
Oh, I remember that...

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:14.160
With Barcgal's skill, I call the 
Future Knight, Llew, from my deck!

00:11:14.160 --> 00:11:16.610
And then, I use Llew's Counterblast!

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:18.970
Stand up, my avatar!

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:20.760
Superior Ride...

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.670
Blaster Blade!

00:11:23.910 --> 00:11:26.530
I have no idea what's going on...

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:31.310
The gist is, no matter what Aichi's plan 
of attack, she's been one step ahead.

00:11:31.310 --> 00:11:32.420
One step ahead?

00:11:32.420 --> 00:11:34.780
From the first turn!

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:36.010
Whaaat?!

00:11:36.010 --> 00:11:39.850
You mean Tokura is psychic?!

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.080
Do you want her autograph?

00:11:43.690 --> 00:11:47.120
No, Misaki is, um...

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:49.890
She has a great memory, right?

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:56.710
After all, you even remember how I 
played during one match at regionals.

00:11:56.710 --> 00:11:58.760
W-Well, sure...

00:11:58.760 --> 00:12:02.910
A good memory, huh? I've got that too, right?

00:12:02.910 --> 00:12:04.740
I suppose so...

00:12:04.740 --> 00:12:08.760
I see! Come to think of it, you 
remembered Ren's deck perfectly, too!

00:12:08.760 --> 00:12:10.640
That's amazing, Misaki!

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:11.750
Not really...

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:14.370
It's not like I <i>try</i> to remember...

00:12:14.610 --> 00:12:16.380
Then you just remember it naturally?

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:18.040
That's even more impressive!

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.710
It's a real talent!

00:12:19.710 --> 00:12:21.210
We're in the middle of a fight!

00:12:21.460 --> 00:12:23.390
Right!

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:27.220
Um, I call the Little Sage, Marron!

00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:33.410
I attack with Wingal, boosted by Barcgal!

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:39.830
Drive check!

00:12:40.650 --> 00:12:43.200
Here we go! Come on, grade 3!

00:12:43.200 --> 00:12:46.840
Wrong! Right now, he wants a grade 2!

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:47.700
Why?

00:12:49.980 --> 00:12:51.400
Damage check.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:55.900
I attack with Marron, boosted by Flogal!

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.770
I guard with Dream Eater!

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:03.590
That's the end of my turn.

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.830
I stand and draw.

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.570
I ride CEO Amaterasu!

00:13:17.840 --> 00:13:19.920
That's amazing, Misaki!

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:21.790
"Amazing"? I fail to see it.

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:24.530
I activate Amaterasu's skill!

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.520
Soulcharge...

00:13:29.820 --> 00:13:32.290
I'm putting this card at 
the bottom of the deck.

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:38.050
I call Silent Tom and the 
Oracle Guardian, Wiseman.

00:13:42.190 --> 00:13:43.760
Wiseman attacks!

00:13:48.140 --> 00:13:48.920
Next!

00:13:49.670 --> 00:13:52.790
I attack with Amaterasu, boosted by Gemini!

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:01.160
Twin drive check.

00:14:01.160 --> 00:14:02.280
First...

00:14:03.090 --> 00:14:04.200
Second...

00:14:06.170 --> 00:14:07.960
Critical trigger.

00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:10.680
I add +5000 to the power of Silent Tom.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:12.480
And you take 2 damage.

00:14:23.600 --> 00:14:25.740
Silent Tom attacks!

00:14:32.870 --> 00:14:34.100
The fourth card...

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.980
He sure is taking a beating...

00:14:36.980 --> 00:14:38.370
4 damage...

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:40.190
But now he's got enough cards for...

00:14:41.810 --> 00:14:42.690
Misaki...?

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:45.270
I stand and draw!

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:47.940
With Barcgal's skill...

00:14:49.710 --> 00:14:52.000
I call Llew from my deck!

00:14:54.670 --> 00:14:58.940
Come to think of it, the last time I 
had a Cardfight with Misaki here...

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:04.060
it was Misaki's first fight,

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:06.900
but her understanding of 
the cards was perfect.

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:11.330
You defeated me completely, remember?

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.480
Come on, just go.

00:15:15.480 --> 00:15:16.320
Sure.

00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:20.070
Misaki sees right through me...

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:23.430
but there must be some way I 
can turn the tables on her.

00:15:24.260 --> 00:15:27.070
Future Knight Llew's Counterblast!

00:15:27.070 --> 00:15:29.630
I pay the cost, moving the card to the Soul!

00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.910
I move Barcgal and Flogal, too!

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:35.410
Superior Ride!

00:15:35.650 --> 00:15:37.520
Blaster Blade!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:44.880
Blaster Blade's Counterblast!

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:51.640
I send Silent Tom off the field!

00:15:58.770 --> 00:16:00.490
I move Marron to the rear-guard.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:05.040
And then I call the Knight of the Rose, 
Morgana and Transporter of Good Luck, Epona!

00:16:07.270 --> 00:16:10.610
I attack with Blaster 
Blade, boosted by Epona!

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.300
Drive trigger check!

00:16:19.970 --> 00:16:21.750
Damage trigger check.

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:25.150
I attack with Morgana, boosted by Marron!

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:30.000
I guard with Nike!

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:32.970
My turn is over.

00:16:33.430 --> 00:16:35.590
Now, the damage is 4 to 4...

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:36.700
but...

00:16:36.700 --> 00:16:38.820
He doesn't have any grade 3s!

00:16:38.820 --> 00:16:39.850
Oh, come on...

00:16:39.850 --> 00:16:42.060
Or, actually, you're right...

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.630
It's because he was slow 
getting a grade 2 out there.

00:16:44.630 --> 00:16:46.620
I stand and...

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:47.770
draw.

00:16:52.270 --> 00:16:56.050
Dream Eater! Its power 
and shield are both 5000!

00:16:57.140 --> 00:16:58.740
That's great, right?!

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:10.750
Amaterasu's skill... Soulcharge...

00:17:11.360 --> 00:17:14.640
I put the top card of my 
deck...on the bottom...

00:17:15.080 --> 00:17:16.730
I call Luck Bird!

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:19.850
I drop two cards for Soulblast!

00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:21.920
I draw one card.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:26.450
I call Wiseman.

00:17:27.630 --> 00:17:30.860
I attack with Wiseman, boosted by Luck Bird!

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:36.290
I guard with Llew!

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:43.320
You know something...

00:17:43.940 --> 00:17:49.040
If she'd used her power of recall 
in actual fights all along,

00:17:49.040 --> 00:17:53.050
by now she'd have been an incredibly 
strong Vanguard Fighter.

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:55.690
That's for sure...

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:57.330
What a waste!

00:17:59.990 --> 00:18:02.960
Next time, I'll teach you how to play.

00:18:02.960 --> 00:18:03.830
Yeah!

00:18:04.790 --> 00:18:06.510
Mind the store while we're gone!

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:10.100
Okay! It'll be no problem!

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:11.940
Be a good girl!

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:13.820
See you later!

00:18:16.140 --> 00:18:17.570
Bye-bye!

00:18:28.370 --> 00:18:29.670
I know!

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:33.850
You're really lucky. I have 
a pretty short memory...

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:37.650
Awesome! Shame on you for keeping 
quiet about it all this time!

00:18:38.030 --> 00:18:43.640
If we can turn the power of Misaki's memory 
into a weapon, Brother, Q4 will be in great shape!

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:44.150
Yep!

00:18:46.220 --> 00:18:47.490
Misaki...?

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:51.290
There are some things I 
don't want to remember...

00:18:52.540 --> 00:18:54.670
Gemini boosts Amaterasu...

00:18:54.670 --> 00:18:56.640
and she attacks Blaster Blade!

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:03.600
Man! And after Dad put it together for me!

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:04.300
Bad cat!

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:08.330
Mom and Dad sure are late...

00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:12.720
They promised to teach 
me how to Cardfight today...

00:19:14.500 --> 00:19:16.260
Misaki! Something terrible's happened!

00:19:16.260 --> 00:19:18.090
It's your Mom and Dad...!

00:19:23.660 --> 00:19:24.850
Twin drive...

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:26.890
First check...

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.030
Dad!

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.960
Mom!!

00:19:58.660 --> 00:20:00.080
Second check!

00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:04.940
Critical trigger! I give 
+5000 to Amaterasu's power!

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:06.700
And the extra critical!

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:22.190
Brother!

00:20:22.190 --> 00:20:23.150
Misaki!

00:20:25.810 --> 00:20:28.330
Shin, are you going to run the store?

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:34.500
There's no way I would close my 
aunt and uncle's beloved store.

00:20:35.310 --> 00:20:38.070
You will help me, won't you, Misaki?

00:20:38.780 --> 00:20:39.990
No.

00:20:42.660 --> 00:20:44.740
I don't know how!

00:20:45.250 --> 00:20:50.880
Dad didn't teach me anything about Cardfight!

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:53.000
Not Dad...

00:20:54.280 --> 00:20:55.990
Or Mom!

00:20:58.020 --> 00:21:00.310
They died before they could!

00:21:01.160 --> 00:21:02.420
Misaki...

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:04.610
It's impossible!

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.290
I can't do it!

00:21:17.110 --> 00:21:19.110
S-She's way strong...

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:21.570
And that memory on top of it...

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:22.840
Wow...

00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:30.790
All right! With Misaki on our side, we can 
totally analyze the decks and fights at Nationals!

00:21:30.790 --> 00:21:33.060
This is a huge advantage!

00:21:34.150 --> 00:21:35.560
Misaki...?

00:21:40.170 --> 00:21:41.020
I can't...

00:21:42.640 --> 00:21:43.780
Misaki...?

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:49.370
I can't fight together 
with you guys anymore...

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:55.180
Misaki...

00:21:55.180 --> 00:21:56.510
H-Hey!

00:21:56.950 --> 00:21:58.570
What was that about?

00:21:58.570 --> 00:21:59.800
You got me...

00:22:01.150 --> 00:22:03.940
Brother, what's wrong with Misaki?

00:22:03.940 --> 00:22:05.700
I-I don't know...

00:22:11.950 --> 00:22:13.160
Misaki...

00:23:51.080 --> 00:23:53.700
Manager, what happened with Misaki?

00:23:53.700 --> 00:23:55.380
Did I do something wrong?

00:23:55.380 --> 00:23:58.890
No, neither you nor Kamui 
did anything wrong, Aichi.

00:23:58.890 --> 00:24:00.750
But Misaki was so...

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:02.670
She said she couldn't fight with us anymore!

00:24:02.670 --> 00:24:03.850
It'll be all right.

00:24:03.850 --> 00:24:06.750
This is probably Misaki's own problem.

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:10.300
She unlocked a door that she has 
to go through sooner or later.

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:13.270
Then it <i>is</i> my fault, isn't it?!

00:24:13.270 --> 00:24:15.380
Next time: Beyond Memories

00:24:15.380 --> 00:24:18.000
She can't picture us being able 
to do something about it together!

00:24:18.000 --> 00:24:19.120
What should I do?!
